        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 20 The Virtual World\nP\u00e1ginas: 397-412\n\u2022 What Is Virtualization Software?  (397)\n\u2022 Installing VirtualBox  (398)\n\u2022 Creating a Virtual Machine  (400)\n\u2022 Customizing a Virtual Machine  (403)\n  \u2022 Changing settings  (404)\n  \u2022 Installing an OS  (406)\n\u2022 Working with the Virtual Machine  (409)\n  \u2022 The Machine menu area  (409)\n  \u2022 The View menu  (410)\n  \u2022 The Devices menu area  (411)\nChapter 20\nThe Virtual World\nW\nhile the term virtual machine sounds an awful lot like air guitar, virtual\nmachines are actually a good thing. They allow you to support multiple\nservers on a single physical machine, saving both space and money.\nThey are quickly becoming all the rage in the corporate world, but can also have a\nplace in the home environment. You can now install more than one Linux distri-\nbution on a single PC, or have Linux and Windows running on the same PC!",
